WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:07.006
AI can make secure code review faster,
broader, and more consistent,

2
00:00:07.086 --> 00:00:10.563
but it does not replace the reviewer.

3
00:00:10.643 --> 00:00:16.925
The reviewer defines the scope, protects
sensitive code and data,

4
00:00:17.005 --> 00:00:21.492
chooses focused prompts, interprets
context,

5
00:00:21.572 --> 00:00:26.283
and decides whether evidence supports a
finding.

6
00:00:26.363 --> 00:00:31.523
AI is strongest when it helps explain
unfamiliar code,

7
00:00:31.603 --> 00:00:38.782
identify likely review patterns, organize
questions, summarize results,

8
00:00:38.862 --> 00:00:44.134
and draft remediation language that a
human can refine.

9
00:00:44.214 --> 00:00:51.281
Strong AI-assisted review workflows start
with authorization and scope.

10
00:00:51.361 --> 00:00:56.857
They prepare by understanding
architecture, data flows,

11
00:00:56.937 --> 00:01:04.341
trust boundaries, authentication,
authorization, dependencies, secrets,

12
00:01:04.421 --> 00:01:06.327
and configuration.

13
00:01:06.407 --> 00:01:11.792
They use focused prompts on manageable
sections of code.

14
00:01:11.872 --> 00:01:17.480
They require the AI to separate evidence
from assumptions.

15
00:01:17.560 --> 00:01:25.412
They verify claims against source code,
tests, configuration, runtime behavior,

16
00:01:25.492 --> 00:01:28.745
and framework-specific context.

17
00:01:28.825 --> 00:01:35.219
They document decisions so the review can
be repeated and defended.

18
00:01:35.299 --> 00:01:41.581
The goal is better security decisions, not
automated confidence.

19
00:01:41.661 --> 00:01:46.596
Treat AI output as a hypothesis until it
is verified.

20
00:01:46.676 --> 00:01:53.070
Treat generated remediation as code that
needs review and testing.

21
00:01:53.150 --> 00:01:57.637
Protect secrets and proprietary
information.

22
00:01:57.717 --> 00:02:05.681
Keep SAST, SCA, pull request, ticketing,
and audit workflows grounded in evidence.

23
00:02:05.761 --> 00:02:13.052
When used this way, AI becomes a practical
assistant for secure engineering:

24
00:02:13.132 --> 00:02:18.180
useful, fast, and bounded by professional
judgment.
